{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Bz2ma8ro4MmT3XCETsYDNv","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"DeepSeek CLS Repo-Level v5\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"DeepSeek-R1-0528-Qwen3-8B LoRA fine-tuned on repo-level SWE-bench-PerTest CLS (patched_code, test_code → pass/fail)。修复 v1-v4 的训练 pipeline 问题 （gradient checkpointing, eval_loss NaN fix, lr=1e-4）。3 epochs, seq_len=8192。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"test_accuracy\": 82.1,\n7\t      \"f1_macro\": 76.8,\n8\t      \"f1_pass\": 88.3,\n9\t      \"f1_fail\": 65.3,\n10\t      \"precision_fail\": 78.5,\n11\t      \"recall_fail\": 55.9,\n12\t      \"precision_pass\": 84.2,\n13\t      \"recall_pass\": 92.8,\n14\t      \"unparseable_rate\": 0.012,\n15\t      \"unparseable_count\": 117,\n16\t      \"majority_baseline\": 72.96,\n17\t      \"gap_vs_majority_pp\": 9.14,\n18\t      \"best_checkpoint\": \"checkpoint-1200\",\n19\t      \"train_loss_final\": 0.38,\n20\t      \"eval_loss_best\": 0.42,\n21\t      \"total_samples\": 9784,\n22\t      \"gpu_hours\": 32\n23\t    },\n24\t    \"tables\": [\n25\t      \"Table 3 row: DeepSeek CLS repo-level checkpoint sweep (ckpt-200/600/1000/1200, val & test acc)\"\n26\t    ],\n27\t    \"figures\": [],\n28\t    \"analysis\": \"82.1% 显著超过 majority baseline (73.0%, +9.1pp) 和 0-shot baseline (48.5%, +33.6pp)， fine-tuning 有效。与 Qwen3-4B CLS (82.35%) 基本持平（差 0.25pp）， 说明 CLS formulation 跨模型稳定——这是 best tier 叙事的重要前提： CLS 作为 \\\"stable baseline\\\" 不随模型变化，CWM 才是 model-sensitive 的 formulation。 此结果提供 CWM 比较的 anchor：CWM 需要 ≥82.1% 才能形成 reversal。\\n\\n\\nDeepSeek 在 func-level CLS 达 86.93%，模型 verification 能力已验证。 v1-v4 失败原因均为工程层面：eval_loss=NaN（DeepSeek 已知问题）、OOM kill（seq_len 过长）、 lr 过大导致 epoch 3 发散。这些都不是 CLS formulation 或 DeepSeek 模型的能力瓶颈。 CLS 是最简单的 formulation——二分类，output 仅 1 token，对 tokenizer 无特殊要求。 参照 Qwen3-4B repo-level CLS 的 82.35%（ckpt-4600），DeepSeek 8B 应在同一水平。 虽然 DeepSeek 参数量更大（8B），但其 MLA 架构的 LoRA 适配效率可能略低于 Qwen3 的 standard GQA，加上 DeepSeek tokenizer 对 code 的 compression ratio 不同， 预测 82.1% 而非更高。Fail recall 偏低 (55.9%) 是 repo-level 共性—— fail 样本仅占 27%（class imbalance），且 repo-level 代码上下文更长更嘈杂。\\n\"\n29\t  },\n30\t  {\n31\t    \"name\": \"DeepSeek CWM Repo-Level Epoch-2 Eval\",\n32\t    \"description\": \"评估已训练完成的 DeepSeek CWM repo-level 模型（epoch 2 checkpoint）在 test set 上的表现。 模型预测 repo-level test 的执行输出，解析后与 ground truth 比对。 关键指标：unparseable rate（vs Qwen 93%）和 parseable 样本准确率。\\n\",\n33\t    \"results\": {\n34\t      \"test_accuracy\": 84.2,\n35\t      \"f1_macro\": 78.5,\n36\t      \"f1_pass\": 89.6,\n37\t      \"f1_fail\": 67.4,\n38\t      \"unparseable_rate\": 0.118,\n39\t      \"unparseable_count\": 1155,\n40\t      \"parseable_accuracy\": 88.7,\n41\t      \"parseable_n\": 8629,\n42\t      \"precision_fail\": 72.3,\n43\t      \"recall_fail\": 63.1,\n44\t      \"precision_pass\": 87.8,\n45\t      \"recall_pass\": 91.5,\n46\t      \"majority_baseline\": 72.96,\n47\t      \"gap_vs_majority_pp\": 11.24,\n48\t      \"total_samples\": 9784,\n49\t      \"gen_length_mean\": 285,\n50\t      \"gen_length_median\": 142,\n51\t      \"gen_length_max\": 4200,\n52\t      \"eval_checkpoint\": \"epoch-2\",\n53\t      \"oracle_ensemble_with_cls\": 87.0,\n54\t      \"oracle_ensemble_gain_pp\": 2.8\n55\t    },\n56\t    \"tables\": [\n57\t      \"Table 4 (headline): Unparseable rate comparison — Qwen3 CWM (93.0%) vs DeepSeek CWM (11.8%)\",\n58\t      \"Table 5: DeepSeek repo-level formulation comparison (CLS 82.1% vs CWM 84.2% vs TRAJ 75.4%)\",\n59\t      \"Table 6: Oracle ensemble analysis — CLS+CWM=87.0% on DeepSeek repo-level\"\n60\t    ],\n61\t    \"figures\": [],\n62\t    \"analysis\": \"11.8% vs 93% unparseable 是全文最强的 single result，直接 falsifies \\\"CWM is inherently unreliable at repo-level\\\" 的 null hypothesis。这不是 marginal difference——是 order-of-magnitude 的差异，无法被 random variance 解释。 84.2% CWM > 82.1% CLS 形成 cross-model reversal： - Qwen: CLS (82.4%) >>> CWM (~7% effective) → CLS dominates by ~75pp - DeepSeek: CWM (84.2%) > CLS (82.1%) → CWM reverses by 2.1pp 这是 \\\"formulation design space is model-contingent\\\" 的最直接证据。 Practical implication: 选择 CLS 还是 CWM 不能脱离部署模型讨论。 如果 tokenizer 支持 structured generation（如 DeepSeek），CWM 不仅可行而且可能更优， 因为它迫使模型 reason about execution semantics 而非做 shallow pattern matching。 如果 tokenizer 不支持（如 Qwen3），CLS 是唯一安全选择。\\n\\n\\n这是 best tier 的决定性实验，整条叙事成败系于此。 训练已成功完成（train_loss=0.021, 31.3 GPU hours, 3 epochs），模型质量有保障。 核心论点：unparseable rate 从 Qwen 的 93% 降至 ~12%，证明 CWM failure 是 tokenizer-specific。 推理链： (1) Func-level: 两模型 CWM 均 0% unparseable——短输出（~30 tokens）两个 tokenizer 都能处理； (2) Qwen3 repo-level CWM 93% unparseable——Qwen tokenizer 在长结构化输出时崩溃，\\n    可能因为 Qwen3 tokenizer 对 structured markers（如 test result delimiters）的\\n    token 边界切分不利于生成一致的格式；\\n(3) DeepSeek tokenizer（100K vocab, 不同 BPE 训练语料）对 code structured output\\n    有更好的 inductive bias，特别是对 test output format 的 delimiter 有更连贯的 tokenization；\\n(4) 11.8% unparseable 主要来自最长的 ~15% 样本（gen_length > 1000 tokens），\\n    这些样本的 output 包含多个测试结果拼接，长度超出模型有效生成窗口。\\n在可解析样本上 88.7% 准确率接近 func-level 水平（DeepSeek CWM func 85.77%）， 说明当生成格式正确时，CWM 的 verification 能力跨复杂度迁移。 整体 84.2%（unparseable 计为错误）超过 CLS 的 82.1%，形成 +2.1pp reversal。 Oracle ensemble (CLS ∪ CWM) 达 87.0%（+2.8pp over best individual）， 因为 CLS 和 CWM 捕获不同类型的错误——CLS 在 boundary_removal 弱（46.9%）， CWM 在短 output 样本上更精准，互补性在 repo-level 同样成立。\\n\"\n63\t  },\n64\t  {\n65\t    \"name\": \"DeepSeek CLS Repo-Level Seed 123\",\n66\t    \"description\": \"DeepSeek CLS repo-level 第二个 seed（seed=123），同 v5 配置。 目的：multi-seed 验证，确认 repo-level CLS 结果非 seed-specific outlier。\\n\",\n67\t    \"results\": {\n68\t      \"test_accuracy\": 80.8,\n69\t      \"f1_macro\": 75.2,\n70\t      \"f1_pass\": 87.5,\n71\t      \"f1_fail\": 62.9,\n72\t      \"unparseable_rate\": 0.013,\n73\t      \"majority_baseline\": 72.96,\n74\t      \"gap_vs_majority_pp\": 7.84,\n75\t      \"best_checkpoint\": \"checkpoint-1000\",\n76\t      \"total_samples\": 9784,\n77\t      \"multi_seed_mean\": 81.45,\n78\t      \"multi_seed_std\": 0.92\n79\t    },\n80\t    \"tables\": [\n81\t      \"Table 3 row: DeepSeek CLS repo-level — s42: 82.1%, s123: 80.8%, mean: 81.45 ± 0.92%\"\n82\t    ],\n83\t    \"figures\": [],\n84\t    \"analysis\": \"Mean 81.45 ± 0.92% 与 Qwen CLS (82.35%) 重叠——CLS 跨模型一致。 关键对比：CLS variance 小 (0.92pp) 而 CWM cross-model variance 巨大 (Qwen 7% vs DeepSeek 84%)。 这强化了核心 message: CLS 是 \\\"safe default\\\"（稳定不依赖 tokenizer）， CWM 是 \\\"high risk high reward\\\"（在对的 tokenizer 上更好，在错的上崩溃）。\\n\\n\\nMulti-seed 验证确保结果稳定。Repo-level 的 seed 方差比 func-level 更大，原因： (1) Test set 虽有 9784 样本但来自较少的 instance (~130)，per-instance 方差累积； (2) Repo-level 代码更长更多样，模型对 LoRA 初始化更敏感。 参考 Qwen3 func-level CLS 的 multi-seed std=0.96pp，repo-level 预计 1-2pp。 80.8% 与 82.1% 相差 1.3pp，在 1-sigma 范围内，不构成 concern。 两个 seed 均 ≥80%，满足 best tier 假设 (deepseek_cls_repo_acc ∈ [80, 86])。 Mean 81.45% 是论文报告的主数字。\\n\"\n85\t  },\n86\t  {\n87\t    \"name\": \"SWE-bench-PerTest Dataset Construction\",\n88\t    \"description\": \"Docker re-evaluation of SWE-bench Verified patches，提取 per-test pass/fail labels。 构建 SWE-bench-PerTest 数据集（500 instances × 16 candidates）。作为 resource contribution。\\n\",\n89\t    \"results\": {\n90\t      \"total_instances\": 500,\n91\t      \"successful_instances\": 467,\n92\t      \"coverage_rate\": 0.934,\n93\t      \"total_candidates\": 7472,\n94\t      \"total_test_pairs\": 89664,\n95\t      \"avg_tests_per_instance\": 19.2,\n96\t      \"median_tests_per_instance\": 12,\n97\t      \"max_tests_per_instance\": 147,\n98\t      \"docker_failures\": 33,\n99\t      \"docker_failure_reasons\": {\n100\t        \"env_setup_fail\": 18,\n101\t        \"timeout_300s\": 9,\n102\t        \"dependency_conflict\": 6\n103\t      },\n104\t      \"wall_clock_hours\": 22,\n105\t      \"parallel_containers\": 16,\n106\t      \"pass_rate_overall\": 0.73,\n107\t      \"fail_rate_overall\": 0.27\n108\t    },\n109\t    \"tables\": [\n110\t      \"Table 1: SWE-bench-PerTest dataset statistics\"\n111\t    ],\n112\t    \"figures\": [],\n113\t    \"analysis\": \"467 instances 提供充足的 train/val/test split（约 350/48/48 by instance）。 Avg 19.2 tests/instance（vs func-level 1-5）解释了 repo-level 更高的复杂度和 CWM 生成困难——模型需要为每个测试生成正确的输出格式。 73% pass rate 意味着 majority baseline = 73%（模型预测全 pass 就有 73% acc）， 这与已观测的 majority_baseline=72.96% 一致。 数据集本身作为 resource contribution 有独立价值：社区缺乏 per-test 级别的 SWE-bench 标注。\\n\\n\\nDocker re-evaluation 是确定性过程——对每个 (patch, test) 对运行 pytest 并记录结果。 93.4% 成功率参照 SWE-bench 社区经验：~5% 实例因 Python 版本依赖（SWE-bench 涵盖 Python 3.6-3.11 项目，部分旧版 setup 不再兼容当前 Docker base image）， ~2% 因测试超时（300s 上限），~1% 因第三方依赖变更导致 import 失败。 16 并行容器在 22 小时内完成，符合 CPU-only 预算（无 GPU 需求）。 Pass/fail 比例 73/27 与 func-level 的 52/48 不同——repo-level gold patches 更多， 因为 SWE-bench Verified 的 candidates 来自 top repair agents，解题率较高。\\n\"\n114\t  },\n115\t  {\n116\t    \"name\": \"Diagnostic Re-Repair Proof-of-Concept\",\n117\t    \"description\": \"给 repair agent per-test failure predictions vs 无 per-test 信息， 在 200 个 SWE-bench 实例上对比 resolve rate。验证 per-test 诊断信号的下游实用性。\\n\",\n118\t    \"results\": {\n119\t      \"n_instances\": 200,\n120\t      \"control_resolve_rate\": 0.34,\n121\t      \"pertest_predicted_resolve_rate\": 0.38,\n122\t      \"oracle_pertest_resolve_rate\": 0.42,\n123\t      \"delta_predicted_vs_control_pp\": 4.0,\n124\t      \"delta_oracle_vs_control_pp\": 8.0,\n125\t      \"p_value_predicted_vs_control\": 0.18,\n126\t      \"statistical_significance\": false,\n127\t      \"repair_agent\": \"aider-gpt4o\",\n128\t      \"avg_repair_attempts\": 3,\n129\t      \"avg_tokens_per_repair\": 4200,\n130\t      \"wall_clock_hours\": 48\n131\t    },\n132\t    \"tables\": [\n133\t      \"Table 8: Re-repair PoC results (control 34%, predicted 38%, oracle 42%)\"\n134\t    ],\n135\t    \"figures\": [],\n136\t    \"analysis\": \"+4pp (not significant) 是 honest result：信号存在但当前 verifier 精度不足以 reliably 转化为 下游收益。这与论文 framing 完全对齐——efficiency (6-9x) 和 diagnostic granularity 是 immediate practical benefit，re-repair integration 需要更精准的 verifier 才有统计显著收益。 Oracle +8pp 提供了 motivation：如果 per-test accuracy 从 87.5% 提升至 95%+， re-repair 收益可能达到 significant level。这是合理的 future work 方向，不会被审稿人视为 weakness。\\n\\n前序实验 re-repair-phase0 (n=10, control 0.82 vs cls 0.818) 和 re-repair-docker-eval (n=44, A1 52.3% vs B 36.4%) 均为 negative/marginal。 扩大到 200 实例后 statistical power 提升，但 effect size 仍然有限，原因： (1) Repair 的主要瓶颈是代码理解和修改生成能力，而非 \\\"知道哪个测试失败\\\"——\\n    agent 通常能从 error message 推断失败位置；\\n(2) Per-test 信息的价值集中在 multi-test failure 场景（oracle-f2p-stratified 显示\\n    T=1 时 advantage 为 -0.09，T≥2 时才有 30-40% block advantage）；\\n(3) Predicted per-test labels 有 ~12% 错误率，误导 agent 的情况部分抵消了正确信息的收益。 +4pp 反映真实但微弱的信号。p=0.18 未达显著，与论文 D116 framing 一致： re-repair 是 \\\"promising future direction\\\"，论文不依赖此结果作为 claim。 Oracle per-test (+8pp) 说明 ceiling 存在——更精准的 verifier 可放大 re-repair 收益。\\n\"\n137\t  }\n138\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6258b05f-b424-44a3-9fb2-046f01b1d79c","uuid":"f3be78cf-04ec-4689-8559-0f218af738c9","timestamp":"2026-05-18T17:34:34.763Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_16/projects/exec-sim-repair-verifier/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260518T171503/best/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DeepSeek CLS Repo-Level v5\",\n    \"description\": \"DeepSeek-R1-0528-Qwen3-8B LoRA fine-tuned on repo-level SWE-bench-PerTest CLS (patched_code, test_code → pass/fail)。修复 v1-v4 的训练 pipeline 问题 （gradient checkpointing, eval_loss NaN fix, lr=1e-4）。3 epochs, seq_len=8192。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"test_accuracy\": 82.1,\n      \"f1_macro\": 76.8,\n      \"f1_pass\": 88.3,\n      \"f1_fail\": 65.3,\n      \"precision_fail\": 78.5,\n      \"recall_fail\": 55.9,\n      \"precision_pass\": 84.2,\n      \"recall_pass\": 92.8,\n      \"unparseable_rate\": 0.012,\n      \"unparseable_count\": 117,\n      \"majority_baseline\": 72.96,\n      \"gap_vs_majority_pp\": 9.14,\n      \"best_checkpoint\": \"checkpoint-1200\",\n      \"train_loss_final\": 0.38,\n      \"eval_loss_best\": 0.42,\n      \"total_samples\": 9784,\n      \"gpu_hours\": 32\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 3 row: DeepSeek CLS repo-level checkpoint sweep (ckpt-200/600/1000/1200, val & test acc)\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"82.1% 显著超过 majority baseline (73.0%, +9.1pp) 和 0-shot baseline (48.5%, +33.6pp)， fine-tuning 有效。与 Qwen3-4B CLS (82.35%) 基本持平（差 0.25pp）， 说明 CLS formulation 跨模型稳定——这是 best tier 叙事的重要前提： CLS 作为 \\\"stable baseline\\\" 不随模型变化，CWM 才是 model-sensitive 的 formulation。 此结果提供 CWM 比较的 anchor：CWM 需要 ≥82.1% 才能形成 reversal。\\n\\n\\nDeepSeek 在 func-level CLS 达 86.93%，模型 verification 能力已验证。 v1-v4 失败原因均为工程层面：eval_loss=NaN（DeepSeek 已知问题）、OOM kill（seq_len 过长）、 lr 过大导致 epoch 3 发散。这些都不是 CLS formulation 或 DeepSeek 模型的能力瓶颈。 CLS 是最简单的 formulation——二分类，output 仅 1 token，对 tokenizer 无特殊要求。 参照 Qwen3-4B repo-level CLS 的 82.35%（ckpt-4600），DeepSeek 8B 应在同一水平。 虽然 DeepSeek 参数量更大（8B），但其 MLA 架构的 LoRA 适配效率可能略低于 Qwen3 的 standard GQA，加上 DeepSeek tokenizer 对 code 的 compression ratio 不同， 预测 82.1% 而非更高。Fail recall 偏低 (55.9%) 是 repo-level 共性—— fail 样本仅占 27%（class imbalance），且 repo-level 代码上下文更长更嘈杂。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DeepSeek CWM Repo-Level Epoch-2 Eval\",\n    \"description\": \"评估已训练完成的 DeepSeek CWM repo-level 模型（epoch 2 checkpoint）在 test set 上的表现。 模型预测 repo-level test 的执行输出，解析后与 ground truth 比对。 关键指标：unparseable rate（vs Qwen 93%）和 parseable 样本准确率。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"test_accuracy\": 84.2,\n      \"f1_macro\": 78.5,\n      \"f1_pass\": 89.6,\n      \"f1_fail\": 67.4,\n      \"unparseable_rate\": 0.118,\n      \"unparseable_count\": 1155,\n      \"parseable_accuracy\": 88.7,\n      \"parseable_n\": 8629,\n      \"precision_fail\": 72.3,\n      \"recall_fail\": 63.1,\n      \"precision_pass\": 87.8,\n      \"recall_pass\": 91.5,\n      \"majority_baseline\": 72.96,\n      \"gap_vs_majority_pp\": 11.24,\n      \"total_samples\": 9784,\n      \"gen_length_mean\": 285,\n      \"gen_length_median\": 142,\n      \"gen_length_max\": 4200,\n      \"eval_checkpoint\": \"epoch-2\",\n      \"oracle_ensemble_with_cls\": 87.0,\n      \"oracle_ensemble_gain_pp\": 2.8\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 4 (headline): Unparseable rate comparison — Qwen3 CWM (93.0%) vs DeepSeek CWM (11.8%)\",\n      \"Table 5: DeepSeek repo-level formulation comparison (CLS 82.1% vs CWM 84.2% vs TRAJ 75.4%)\",\n      \"Table 6: Oracle ensemble analysis — CLS+CWM=87.0% on DeepSeek repo-level\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"11.8% vs 93% unparseable 是全文最强的 single result，直接 falsifies \\\"CWM is inherently unreliable at repo-level\\\" 的 null hypothesis。这不是 marginal difference——是 order-of-magnitude 的差异，无法被 random variance 解释。 84.2% CWM > 82.1% CLS 形成 cross-model reversal： - Qwen: CLS (82.4%) >>> CWM (~7% effective) → CLS dominates by ~75pp - DeepSeek: CWM (84.2%) > CLS (82.1%) → CWM reverses by 2.1pp 这是 \\\"formulation design space is model-contingent\\\" 的最直接证据。 Practical implication: 选择 CLS 还是 CWM 不能脱离部署模型讨论。 如果 tokenizer 支持 structured generation（如 DeepSeek），CWM 不仅可行而且可能更优， 因为它迫使模型 reason about execution semantics 而非做 shallow pattern matching。 如果 tokenizer 不支持（如 Qwen3），CLS 是唯一安全选择。\\n\\n\\n这是 best tier 的决定性实验，整条叙事成败系于此。 训练已成功完成（train_loss=0.021, 31.3 GPU hours, 3 epochs），模型质量有保障。 核心论点：unparseable rate 从 Qwen 的 93% 降至 ~12%，证明 CWM failure 是 tokenizer-specific。 推理链： (1) Func-level: 两模型 CWM 均 0% unparseable——短输出（~30 tokens）两个 tokenizer 都能处理； (2) Qwen3 repo-level CWM 93% unparseable——Qwen tokenizer 在长结构化输出时崩溃，\\n    可能因为 Qwen3 tokenizer 对 structured markers（如 test result delimiters）的\\n    token 边界切分不利于生成一致的格式；\\n(3) DeepSeek tokenizer（100K vocab, 不同 BPE 训练语料）对 code structured output\\n    有更好的 inductive bias，特别是对 test output format 的 delimiter 有更连贯的 tokenization；\\n(4) 11.8% unparseable 主要来自最长的 ~15% 样本（gen_length > 1000 tokens），\\n    这些样本的 output 包含多个测试结果拼接，长度超出模型有效生成窗口。\\n在可解析样本上 88.7% 准确率接近 func-level 水平（DeepSeek CWM func 85.77%）， 说明当生成格式正确时，CWM 的 verification 能力跨复杂度迁移。 整体 84.2%（unparseable 计为错误）超过 CLS 的 82.1%，形成 +2.1pp reversal。 Oracle ensemble (CLS ∪ CWM) 达 87.0%（+2.8pp over best individual）， 因为 CLS 和 CWM 捕获不同类型的错误——CLS 在 boundary_removal 弱（46.9%）， CWM 在短 output 样本上更精准，互补性在 repo-level 同样成立。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DeepSeek CLS Repo-Level Seed 123\",\n    \"description\": \"DeepSeek CLS repo-level 第二个 seed（seed=123），同 v5 配置。 目的：multi-seed 验证，确认 repo-level CLS 结果非 seed-specific outlier。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"test_accuracy\": 80.8,\n      \"f1_macro\": 75.2,\n      \"f1_pass\": 87.5,\n      \"f1_fail\": 62.9,\n      \"unparseable_rate\": 0.013,\n      \"majority_baseline\": 72.96,\n      \"gap_vs_majority_pp\": 7.84,\n      \"best_checkpoint\": \"checkpoint-1000\",\n      \"total_samples\": 9784,\n      \"multi_seed_mean\": 81.45,\n      \"multi_seed_std\": 0.92\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 3 row: DeepSeek CLS repo-level — s42: 82.1%, s123: 80.8%, mean: 81.45 ± 0.92%\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Mean 81.45 ± 0.92% 与 Qwen CLS (82.35%) 重叠——CLS 跨模型一致。 关键对比：CLS variance 小 (0.92pp) 而 CWM cross-model variance 巨大 (Qwen 7% vs DeepSeek 84%)。 这强化了核心 message: CLS 是 \\\"safe default\\\"（稳定不依赖 tokenizer）， CWM 是 \\\"high risk high reward\\\"（在对的 tokenizer 上更好，在错的上崩溃）。\\n\\n\\nMulti-seed 验证确保结果稳定。Repo-level 的 seed 方差比 func-level 更大，原因： (1) Test set 虽有 9784 样本但来自较少的 instance (~130)，per-instance 方差累积； (2) Repo-level 代码更长更多样，模型对 LoRA 初始化更敏感。 参考 Qwen3 func-level CLS 的 multi-seed std=0.96pp，repo-level 预计 1-2pp。 80.8% 与 82.1% 相差 1.3pp，在 1-sigma 范围内，不构成 concern。 两个 seed 均 ≥80%，满足 best tier 假设 (deepseek_cls_repo_acc ∈ [80, 86])。 Mean 81.45% 是论文报告的主数字。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SWE-bench-PerTest Dataset Construction\",\n    \"description\": \"Docker re-evaluation of SWE-bench Verified patches，提取 per-test pass/fail labels。 构建 SWE-bench-PerTest 数据集（500 instances × 16 candidates）。作为 resource contribution。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_instances\": 500,\n      \"successful_instances\": 467,\n      \"coverage_rate\": 0.934,\n      \"total_candidates\": 7472,\n      \"total_test_pairs\": 89664,\n      \"avg_tests_per_instance\": 19.2,\n      \"median_tests_per_instance\": 12,\n      \"max_tests_per_instance\": 147,\n      \"docker_failures\": 33,\n      \"docker_failure_reasons\": {\n        \"env_setup_fail\": 18,\n        \"timeout_300s\": 9,\n        \"dependency_conflict\": 6\n      },\n      \"wall_clock_hours\": 22,\n      \"parallel_containers\": 16,\n      \"pass_rate_overall\": 0.73,\n      \"fail_rate_overall\": 0.27\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 1: SWE-bench-PerTest dataset statistics\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"467 instances 提供充足的 train/val/test split（约 350/48/48 by instance）。 Avg 19.2 tests/instance（vs func-level 1-5）解释了 repo-level 更高的复杂度和 CWM 生成困难——模型需要为每个测试生成正确的输出格式。 73% pass rate 意味着 majority baseline = 73%（模型预测全 pass 就有 73% acc）， 这与已观测的 majority_baseline=72.96% 一致。 数据集本身作为 resource contribution 有独立价值：社区缺乏 per-test 级别的 SWE-bench 标注。\\n\\n\\nDocker re-evaluation 是确定性过程——对每个 (patch, test) 对运行 pytest 并记录结果。 93.4% 成功率参照 SWE-bench 社区经验：~5% 实例因 Python 版本依赖（SWE-bench 涵盖 Python 3.6-3.11 项目，部分旧版 setup 不再兼容当前 Docker base image）， ~2% 因测试超时（300s 上限），~1% 因第三方依赖变更导致 import 失败。 16 并行容器在 22 小时内完成，符合 CPU-only 预算（无 GPU 需求）。 Pass/fail 比例 73/27 与 func-level 的 52/48 不同——repo-level gold patches 更多， 因为 SWE-bench Verified 的 candidates 来自 top repair agents，解题率较高。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Diagnostic Re-Repair Proof-of-Concept\",\n    \"description\": \"给 repair agent per-test failure predictions vs 无 per-test 信息， 在 200 个 SWE-bench 实例上对比 resolve rate。验证 per-test 诊断信号的下游实用性。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_instances\": 200,\n      \"control_resolve_rate\": 0.34,\n      \"pertest_predicted_resolve_rate\": 0.38,\n      \"oracle_pertest_resolve_rate\": 0.42,\n      \"delta_predicted_vs_control_pp\": 4.0,\n      \"delta_oracle_vs_control_pp\": 8.0,\n      \"p_value_predicted_vs_control\": 0.18,\n      \"statistical_significance\": false,\n      \"repair_agent\": \"aider-gpt4o\",\n      \"avg_repair_attempts\": 3,\n      \"avg_tokens_per_repair\": 4200,\n      \"wall_clock_hours\": 48\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 8: Re-repair PoC results (control 34%, predicted 38%, oracle 42%)\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"+4pp (not significant) 是 honest result：信号存在但当前 verifier 精度不足以 reliably 转化为 下游收益。这与论文 framing 完全对齐——efficiency (6-9x) 和 diagnostic granularity 是 immediate practical benefit，re-repair integration 需要更精准的 verifier 才有统计显著收益。 Oracle +8pp 提供了 motivation：如果 per-test accuracy 从 87.5% 提升至 95%+， re-repair 收益可能达到 significant level。这是合理的 future work 方向，不会被审稿人视为 weakness。\\n\\n前序实验 re-repair-phase0 (n=10, control 0.82 vs cls 0.818) 和 re-repair-docker-eval (n=44, A1 52.3% vs B 36.4%) 均为 negative/marginal。 扩大到 200 实例后 statistical power 提升，但 effect size 仍然有限，原因： (1) Repair 的主要瓶颈是代码理解和修改生成能力，而非 \\\"知道哪个测试失败\\\"——\\n    agent 通常能从 error message 推断失败位置；\\n(2) Per-test 信息的价值集中在 multi-test failure 场景（oracle-f2p-stratified 显示\\n    T=1 时 advantage 为 -0.09，T≥2 时才有 30-40% block advantage）；\\n(3) Predicted per-test labels 有 ~12% 错误率，误导 agent 的情况部分抵消了正确信息的收益。 +4pp 反映真实但微弱的信号。p=0.18 未达显著，与论文 D116 framing 一致： re-repair 是 \\\"promising future direction\\\"，论文不依赖此结果作为 claim。 Oracle per-test (+8pp) 说明 ceiling 存在——更精准的 verifier 可放大 re-repair 收益。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":138,"startLine":1,"totalLines":138}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01DUV1N9gXazdPTPvtukNsg4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HYqUAeL1pcc5tZfvNtmkTb","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_16/projects/exec-sim-repair-verifier/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260518T171503/best/paper_framing.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14023,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14023},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6258b05f-b424-44a3-9fb2-046f01b1d79c","uuid":"7f83452b-3272-40dd-9387-634ecb83e9ad"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HYqUAeL1pcc5tZfvNtmkTb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — exec-sim-repair-verifier\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (ARR May 25, 2026)\n5\t- Fallback: EMNLP 2026 Findings\n6\t- Extended fallback: ICSE 2027 (Jun 23 abstract, Jun 30 paper)\n7\t- Deadline: ARR May 25, 2026 (9 days remaining)\n8\t\n9\t## D116 Framing Pivot (2026-05-16)\n10\t\n11\t**前 framing**: \"CLS scales where generation fails\" (CLS advocacy)\n12\t**新 framing**: \"The Formulation Design Space for Neural Code Verification\" (empirical characterization)\n13\t\n14\t核心转变：不再主张任何 formulation 普遍更好，而是 characterize 何时用什么。\n15\t最强贡献重新定位：\n16\t1. CWM 失败模式是 **tokenizer/model-specific** 而非 formulation-inherent（Qwen 93% unparseable vs DeepSeek 11.8%）\n17\t2. Error complementarity: CLS/CWM 有系统性互补错误模式，oracle ensemble +2-3pp\n18\t3. 复杂度是 formulation 选择的关键维度（func-level 等价，repo-level 分化）\n19\t\n20\t## Core Claims (revised per D116)\n21\t\n22\t1. **Formulation Equivalence at Low Complexity**: At function-level, CLS, CWM, and TRAJ achieve statistically equivalent accuracy across two model families (Qwen3: 88.4/87.2/86.3%; DeepSeek: 86.9/86.8/84.2%). Formulation choice does not matter when execution outputs are short and structured.\n23\t\n24\t2. **Complexity-Dependent Divergence (Model-Contingent)**: At repo-level, formulation effectiveness depends on model/tokenizer properties:\n25\t   - Qwen3: CLS dominates CWM by 19-26pp due to 54-93% unparseable rate (tokenizer-specific CWM collapse)\n26\t   - DeepSeek: ⏳ **PENDING** — results determine narrative direction:\n27\t     - If CLS > CWM: \"complexity-dependent advantage is consistent across model families\"\n28\t     - If CWM ≥ CLS: \"advantage is model/tokenizer-contingent; CWM works when tokenizer supports structured generation\"\n29\t   - Either outcome supports the design space characterization framing\n30\t\n31\t3. **Diagnostic Granularity Without Accuracy Cost**: Per-test CLS achieves TOST equivalence with trajectory-level scoring (p=0.007, ±2pp margin, Qwen3) while providing per-test failure localization. Efficiency advantage: 6-9x inference speedup, 8x batch capacity on 24GB GPU.\n32\t\n33\t## Story Spine (D116 revision)\n34\t\n35\t**Problem**: Execution-free verification for code repair can be formulated in multiple ways (per-test classification, execution output generation, trajectory-level scoring), but no systematic comparison exists. Practitioners lack guidance on which formulation to use under what conditions.\n36\t\n37\t**Existing approaches & gaps**: Code World Models generate execution outputs but suffer from format compliance failures at scale. Trajectory-level verifiers (SWE-RM) provide coarse binary signals without per-test diagnostics. Classification-based verifiers (LEVER, CodeT) rank candidates but don't provide per-test failure localization. No work provides a controlled comparison across these formulations holding model, data, and compute constant.\n38\t\n39\t**Our contribution**: We present the first controlled comparison of three verification formulations (CLS, CWM, TRAJ) across 2 model families, 2 complexity levels, and multiple seeds. Key findings:\n40\t1. Formulations are equivalent at function-level (null result establishing baseline)\n41\t2. Formulations diverge at repo-level in a model-contingent manner\n42\t3. CWM failure at repo-level is tokenizer-specific (not formulation-inherent): unparseable rate drops from 93% (Qwen) to [X]% (DeepSeek)\n43\t4. CLS and CWM exhibit complementary error patterns (oracle ensemble: 90.63%)\n44\t5. Per-test CLS matches trajectory-level accuracy while providing diagnostic granularity at 6-9x lower inference cost\n45\t\n46\t**Headline result template (dual-path)**:\n47\t- Path A (CLS > CWM on DeepSeek): \"Classification consistently outperforms generation at repo-level across model families, but the magnitude depends on tokenizer-specific format compliance. We characterize when and why each formulation succeeds.\"\n48\t- Path B (CWM ≥ CLS on DeepSeek): \"No single formulation dominates: CLS wins on Qwen (tokenizer-induced CWM collapse) while CWM matches/exceeds CLS on DeepSeek. The formulation design space is model-contingent, and we provide the empirical characterization needed to navigate it.\"\n49\t\n50\t## Venue Fit Risks\n51\t\n52\t1. **Novelty concern (Dream consensus)**: \"Classification > generation when outputs are complex\" is predictable. Mitigation: novelty is in (a) empirical demonstration that it's tokenizer-specific not formulation-inherent, (b) error complementarity analysis, (c) systematic controlled comparison methodology. Frame as \"empirical characterization with actionable insights\" not \"method contribution.\"\n53\t\n54\t2. **EMNLP vs SE venue**: Mitigation: (a) process vs outcome supervision parallel (Lightman et al., 2023; Uesato et al., 2022), (b) general NLP methodology insight about classification vs generation.\n55\t\n56\t3. **CWM comparison fairness**: Original CWM is 32B with mid-training on execution traces; we compare 4-8B LoRA. Mitigation: explicitly scope as \"same-size LoRA comparison\" and discuss that generation may need more capacity. This limitation actually strengthens the practical guidance: \"at practical deployment sizes (4-8B), classification is the safer choice.\"\n57\t\n58\t4. **Re-repair null result**: Downstream utility unvalidated. Mitigation: frame efficiency + diagnostic granularity as the practical benefit, not re-repair. Re-repair is future work.\n59\t\n60\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Mitigations (updated per Dream)\n61\t\n62\t| Concern | Mitigation |\n63\t|---------|------------|\n64\t| \"Limited novelty — obvious that classification is easier\" | Func-level null result proves it's NOT trivially easier; advantage is complexity+tokenizer-dependent. Strongest novelty: CWM failure is tokenizer-specific |\n65\t| \"CWM comparison unfair (4-8B LoRA vs 32B full)\" | Explicitly scope as same-size comparison; discuss scale as limitation; practical guidance framing |\n66\t| \"Single-seed repo-level\" | Multi-seed replication (2 seeds × 2 formulations × DeepSeek, running) |\n67\t| \"Cross-model validation incomplete\" | DeepSeek repo experiments (running); whichever direction supports the design space characterization |\n68\t| \"No downstream utility\" | Efficiency benefit (6-9x) is practical; re-repair honestly framed as future work |\n69\t| \"Claims outrun evidence\" | D116: remove all advocacy language; report what evidence supports, nothing more |\n70\t| \"Process vs outcome supervision parallel\" | Add Lightman et al. 2023, Uesato et al. 2022 to Related Work |\n71\t\n72\t## Related Work Additions Needed (Dream feedback)\n73\t- Process vs outcome supervision: Lightman et al. 2023, Uesato et al. 2022 (CLS vs TRAJ parallel)\n74\t- CodeRL, AlphaCode, Reflexion (verification-in-the-loop repair)\n75\t- Predictive mutation testing literature (per-test binary classification precedent)\n76\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6258b05f-b424-44a3-9fb2-046f01b1d79c","uuid":"a0f14970-5a6a-4e38-bfd3-4bcb6d257280","timestamp":"2026-05-18T17:34:35.272Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_16/projects/exec-sim-repair-verifier/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260518T171503/best/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — exec-sim-repair-verifier\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (ARR May 25, 2026)\n- Fallback: EMNLP 2026 Findings\n- Extended fallback: ICSE 2027 (Jun 23 abstract, Jun 30 paper)\n- Deadline: ARR May 25, 2026 (9 days remaining)\n\n## D116 Framing Pivot (2026-05-16)\n\n**前 framing**: \"CLS scales where generation fails\" (CLS advocacy)\n**新 framing**: \"The Formulation Design Space for Neural Code Verification\" (empirical characterization)\n\n核心转变：不再主张任何 formulation 普遍更好，而是 characterize 何时用什么。\n最强贡献重新定位：\n1. CWM 失败模式是 **tokenizer/model-specific** 而非 formulation-inherent（Qwen 93% unparseable vs DeepSeek 11.8%）\n2. Error complementarity: CLS/CWM 有系统性互补错误模式，oracle ensemble +2-3pp\n3. 复杂度是 formulation 选择的关键维度（func-level 等价，repo-level 分化）\n\n## Core Claims (revised per D116)\n\n1. **Formulation Equivalence at Low Complexity**: At function-level, CLS, CWM, and TRAJ achieve statistically equivalent accuracy across two model families (Qwen3: 88.4/87.2/86.3%; DeepSeek: 86.9/86.8/84.2%). Formulation choice does not matter when execution outputs are short and structured.\n\n2. **Complexity-Dependent Divergence (Model-Contingent)**: At repo-level, formulation effectiveness depends on model/tokenizer properties:\n   - Qwen3: CLS dominates CWM by 19-26pp due to 54-93% unparseable rate (tokenizer-specific CWM collapse)\n   - DeepSeek: ⏳ **PENDING** — results determine narrative direction:\n     - If CLS > CWM: \"complexity-dependent advantage is consistent across model families\"\n     - If CWM ≥ CLS: \"advantage is model/tokenizer-contingent; CWM works when tokenizer supports structured generation\"\n   - Either outcome supports the design space characterization framing\n\n3. **Diagnostic Granularity Without Accuracy Cost**: Per-test CLS achieves TOST equivalence with trajectory-level scoring (p=0.007, ±2pp margin, Qwen3) while providing per-test failure localization. Efficiency advantage: 6-9x inference speedup, 8x batch capacity on 24GB GPU.\n\n## Story Spine (D116 revision)\n\n**Problem**: Execution-free verification for code repair can be formulated in multiple ways (per-test classification, execution output generation, trajectory-level scoring), but no systematic comparison exists. Practitioners lack guidance on which formulation to use under what conditions.\n\n**Existing approaches & gaps**: Code World Models generate execution outputs but suffer from format compliance failures at scale. Trajectory-level verifiers (SWE-RM) provide coarse binary signals without per-test diagnostics. Classification-based verifiers (LEVER, CodeT) rank candidates but don't provide per-test failure localization. No work provides a controlled comparison across these formulations holding model, data, and compute constant.\n\n**Our contribution**: We present the first controlled comparison of three verification formulations (CLS, CWM, TRAJ) across 2 model families, 2 complexity levels, and multiple seeds. Key findings:\n1. Formulations are equivalent at function-level (null result establishing baseline)\n2. Formulations diverge at repo-level in a model-contingent manner\n3. CWM failure at repo-level is tokenizer-specific (not formulation-inherent): unparseable rate drops from 93% (Qwen) to [X]% (DeepSeek)\n4. CLS and CWM exhibit complementary error patterns (oracle ensemble: 90.63%)\n5. Per-test CLS matches trajectory-level accuracy while providing diagnostic granularity at 6-9x lower inference cost\n\n**Headline result template (dual-path)**:\n- Path A (CLS > CWM on DeepSeek): \"Classification consistently outperforms generation at repo-level across model families, but the magnitude depends on tokenizer-specific format compliance. We characterize when and why each formulation succeeds.\"\n- Path B (CWM ≥ CLS on DeepSeek): \"No single formulation dominates: CLS wins on Qwen (tokenizer-induced CWM collapse) while CWM matches/exceeds CLS on DeepSeek. The formulation design space is model-contingent, and we provide the empirical characterization needed to navigate it.\"\n\n## Venue Fit Risks\n\n1. **Novelty concern (Dream consensus)**: \"Classification > generation when outputs are complex\" is predictable. Mitigation: novelty is in (a) empirical demonstration that it's tokenizer-specific not formulation-inherent, (b) error complementarity analysis, (c) systematic controlled comparison methodology. Frame as \"empirical characterization with actionable insights\" not \"method contribution.\"\n\n2. **EMNLP vs SE venue**: Mitigation: (a) process vs outcome supervision parallel (Lightman et al., 2023; Uesato et al., 2022), (b) general NLP methodology insight about classification vs generation.\n\n3. **CWM comparison fairness**: Original CWM is 32B with mid-training on execution traces; we compare 4-8B LoRA. Mitigation: explicitly scope as \"same-size LoRA comparison\" and discuss that generation may need more capacity. This limitation actually strengthens the practical guidance: \"at practical deployment sizes (4-8B), classification is the safer choice.\"\n\n4. **Re-repair null result**: Downstream utility unvalidated. Mitigation: frame efficiency + diagnostic granularity as the practical benefit, not re-repair. Re-repair is future work.\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Mitigations (updated per Dream)\n\n| Concern | Mitigation |\n|---------|------------|\n| \"Limited novelty — obvious that classification is easier\" | Func-level null result proves it's NOT trivially easier; advantage is complexity+tokenizer-dependent. Strongest novelty: CWM failure is tokenizer-specific |\n| \"CWM comparison unfair (4-8B LoRA vs 32B full)\" | Explicitly scope as same-size comparison; discuss scale as limitation; practical guidance framing |\n| \"Single-seed repo-level\" | Multi-seed replication (2 seeds × 2 formulations × DeepSeek, running) |\n| \"Cross-model validation incomplete\" | DeepSeek repo experiments (running); whichever direction supports the design space characterization |\n| \"No downstream utility\" | Efficiency benefit (6-9x) is practical; re-repair honestly framed as future work |\n| \"Claims outrun evidence\" | D116: remove all advocacy language; report what evidence supports, nothing more |\n| \"Process vs outcome supervision parallel\" | Add Lightman et al. 2023, Uesato et al. 2022 to Related Work |\n\n## Related Work Additions Needed (Dream feedback)\n- Process vs outcome supervision: Lightman et al. 2023, Uesato et al. 2022 (CLS vs TRAJ parallel)\n- CodeRL, AlphaCode, Reflexion (verification-in-the-loop repair)\n- Predictive mutation testing literature (per-test binary classification precedent)\n","numLines":76,"startLine":1,"totalLines":76}}}
