evel results from the framing document to complete Table 2. Looking at my table structure, I need to renumber them sequentially for the paper rather than using the experiment references — so I'm consolidating everything into a clean seven-table structure. I notice the experiment data references a \"TRAJ 75.4%\" result for DeepSeek repo-level that should appear in Table 5, but I'm not seeing it in the JSON results yet, so I need to track down where that number comes from.\n\nFor the checkpoint sweep table, I only have the final results from checkpoint 1200 rather than individual checkpoint scores, so I'll adjust that to show the multi-seed results I actually have. Now I'm ready to write out the full LaTeX paper with a clean article format.\n\nWriting the LaTeX document...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":903,"cache_read_input_tokens":32928,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":903},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6258b05f-b424-44a3-9fb2-046f01b1d79c","uuid":"e51778b8-09e4-4874-9ba2-89bccc14ce8b"}
